From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: prepare MSM8226 DSI parents during rate changes

The first native modeset on SM-T531 times out updating pclk0 and byte0
RCGs. Firmware leaves these roots on, but the DSI host changes rates
before preparing the PLL. Prepare the selected parent around RCG clock
operations using CCF's existing parent-enable flag, limited to MSM8226.

This follows the mechanism used by upstream commit acf7a91d0b0e
("clk: qcom: dispcc-sm8250: Enable parents for pixel clocks") and the
SDM660 v2 discussion by Fabricio Akio on 2026-10-02:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2610.0/04606.html
The 28nm PLL and byte root must still be validated on this device; this
patch does not establish working native display or PLL power management.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8974.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8974.c
index 07ce89502..b45b28d10 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8974.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8974.c
@@ -2739,10 +2739,19 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, mmcc_msm8974_match_table);
 static void msm8226_clock_override(void)
 {
 	static struct clk_init_data axi_init;
+	static struct clk_init_data pixel_init;
+	static struct clk_init_data byte_init;
 
 	axi_init = *oxilicx_axi_clk.clkr.hw.init;
 	axi_init.flags |= CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT;
 	oxilicx_axi_clk.clkr.hw.init = &axi_init;
+	/* Boot firmware can leave the RCG on while the DSI PLL is stopped. */
+	pixel_init = *pclk0_clk_src.clkr.hw.init;
+	pixel_init.flags |= CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE;
+	pclk0_clk_src.clkr.hw.init = &pixel_init;
+	byte_init = *byte0_clk_src.clkr.hw.init;
+	byte_init.flags |= CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE;
+	byte0_clk_src.clkr.hw.init = &byte_init;
 	mmss_axi_clk_src.freq_tbl = ftbl_mmss_axi_clk_msm8226;
 	vfe0_clk_src.freq_tbl = ftbl_camss_vfe_vfe0_clk_msm8226;
 	mdp_clk_src.freq_tbl = ftbl_mdss_mdp_clk_msm8226;
